{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"Recheck R-002 against sandbox_prefix and other claims in the selected notes and docs.","verdict":"block","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"R-003","severity":"low","summary":"The docs say credential-shaped workspace files are denied to file tools, but the permission settings deny only .env, .pem, and .key patterns. Other filenames found by _credential_files are masked at the OS level, but are not explicitly denied by the file-tool rules.","evidence":["docs/claude-task-executor.md: “Credential-shaped workspace files are masked from shell reads as well as denied to file tools.”","scripts/task_run/task_run_claude_sandbox.py: _settings adds Read denies for **/.env, **/.env.*, **/*.pem, and **/*.key; its allow rules include Read(worktree/**).","scripts/task_run/task_run_claude_sandbox.py: _credential_files also finds names such as credentials.json, .netrc, and id_rsa, which sandbox_prefix masks with empty-credential; those names are not added to _settings’ deny rules."] ,"action":"Qualify the claim to distinguish OS masking from file-tool permission denial, or add per-file deny rules for the discovered credential paths and test that behavior."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"R-002: the reachability exceptions omitted exact masked home-file paths.","bin":"resolved","disposition":"The new general wording covers any path the sandbox masks, and “a masked home path” is an example rather than a complete list. sandbox_prefix masks both home directories and individual home files."},{"concern":"Whether arbitrary host Unix socket reachability is covered by integration tests.","bin":"disclosed-test-limit","disposition":"The notes identify the Docker socket test and say other daemon paths and /run/user/<uid> are not pinned; the general reachability statement is supported by the mount setup, not presented as an integration-test result."}],"next_move":"Correct the file-tool denial sentence, then recheck that wording against _settings and its tests.","non_claims":["Review used only the supplied semantic input; no tests or sandbox behavior were executed.","The supplied paths do not include CI configuration, so the statement that CI does not run the real-sandbox tests was not independently checked."]}
